course: dictionary
lesson: 12581
title: One word, two meanings: diner
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A diner can be a person, and it can also be a place. Context tells you which one. «The waiter brought a glass of water to each diner.» Here a diner is a person eating a meal, because a waiter serves people, not buildings.
explain: «At the roadside diner, the family ordered burgers and milkshakes.» Roadside tells you where, and burgers and milkshakes tell you it is a place that serves food. In the USA and Canada, a diner is a small, simple restaurant.
explain: Check the clues before you decide. Ask: is this a person or a place? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «The all-night diner was open until dawn.» A person cannot be open until dawn, so this diner is a place.
fact: A diner is a person who is eating a meal, especially in a restaurant.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a diner is a small, simple restaurant.
fact: A diner there serves cheap meals like burgers, pancakes and milkshakes.
fact: A diner, the place, often has a long counter where customers sit on stools.
fact: Phrases to know: a roadside diner, an all-night diner, diners at the restaurant.
exercise: «Every diner in the restaurant ordered soup.» What is a diner in this sentence? | A bus stop | *A person eating a meal | A type of plate | A small roadside building
exercise: «The roadside diner was full of hungry travellers.» What is a diner in this sentence? | A kind of car | A kitchen cook | A person eating a meal | *A small, simple restaurant
exercise: «The old film showed families eating pancakes in a booth at the diner.» Where did the families eat? | On a train | In the park | *At the diner | In a shop
test: «Lily ordered a milkshake at the all-night diner.» Is the diner a person or a place? | A milkshake | *A place | A waiter | A person
test: The waiter smiled at each diner. What does diner mean here? | A cook in the kitchen | *A person eating a meal | A menu | A glass of water
exam: «The diners at the long counter ordered burgers, and the cook called out the orders.» Which word shows the diners are people eating a meal? | *ordered | Long | counter | cook
